note seed/node/tests/tool-replay.om: replay the round-40 tool transcripts through the Omega Node tool
note and compare every next prompt byte for byte (the seeded-Omega port of tool-replay.py).
note Build: { printf 'om2\n'; cat seed/json/json.om seed/node/tests/drv.om seed/node/tests/tool-replay.om; }
note   | seed/out/omc > build/node/tool-replay
note Usage: tool-replay TOOL OMC ROUND40 OUTDIR. Reads ROUND40/final-selected.json (a list of runs).
note Per run: OUTDIR/<job.id> is removed, ROOT/dirname(job.path) and ROOT/.work made, job.broken written
note to ROOT/job.path unless job.fault is "missing". For every turn but the last the turn's raw answer
note is cut at the first "\nDone.", stripped (Python str.strip whitespace) and parsed as JSON; its tool
note runs as one TOOL process (read_file: read ROOT PATH; omega_check: check ROOT PATH ROOT/.work OMC
note KIND K N A with KIND add 1, mul 2, loop 3 and N job.n or 0; any other tool: replace ROOT PATH OLD
note NEW), stdout captured to OUTDIR/.tool-replay.out, stderr to /dev/null, 120 s deadline. Exit 0 gives
note the OMNT1 record (status, observation, content; content dropped for status 1); another exit gives
note status None and observation "exit N" (N = -signal for a signal). The rebuilt repair.py prompt
note (Task, File, Goal, State, Source, Tool result, Answer) must equal the next turn's prompt; the
note first difference prints "MISMATCH id fault tool status ST REPR" and "  want REPR" (Python repr,
note first and last 200 code points) and fails the run. Summary: TOOL-REPLAY runs= pass= fail=
note actions=; exit 0 when no run failed, 1 otherwise, 2 for bad usage or an unreadable fixture.
note Where tool-replay.py would have raised (missing or mistyped fixture field, style outside 0..50,
note non-integer number, tool timeout, malformed OMNT1 record, field over its buffer), this driver
note fails the run instead: an "ERROR id step" line, or a MISMATCH with status None and observation
note "timeout", "malformed record" or "spawn error". A job id that is empty, ".", ".." or holds '/'
note is refused (ERROR) so OUTDIR/<id> is always a direct child of OUTDIR. repr approximation: code
note points U+0080..U+00A0 and U+00AD print as \xNN, every other non-ASCII code point raw.
note Buffers: raw answer 8192 bytes, prompt and tool stdout 16384, id 1024, path 3072, fault 1024,
note tool name 1024, broken 6144, any path 4095.
note ba (32768 bytes): TOOL 0, OMC 4096, OUTDIR 8192, ROOT 12288, WORK 16384, capture file 20480,
note prompt head 24576, fixture path 28672; their lengths in tra[0..7].
note bj (16384 bytes): id 0, path 1024, fault 4096, tool name 5120, broken 6144, packed argv 12288;
note lengths tra-style in trb: [0] id, [1] path, [2] fault, [3] broken, [4] tool name, [5] broken set.

global tra ulong 8
global trb ulong 8
note trv: [0] style, [1] kind code (1 add, 2 mul, 3 loop, 0 other), [2] k, [3] n, [4] a, [5] n given.
global trv long 8
note trs: [0] status (dvnone = None), [1] obs offset, [2] obs length, [3] content offset,
note [4] content length, [5] next-turn token, [6] packed argv length.
global trs ulong 8
note trn: [0] runs, [1] passed runs, [2] failed runs, [3] tool actions.
global trn ulong 4

text trkjob "job"
text trkid "id"
text trkpath "path"
text trkflt "fault"
text trkkind "kind"
text trkstyl "style"
text trkk "k"
text trkn "n"
text trka "a"
text trkbrok "broken"
text trkturn "turns"
text trkraw "raw"
text trkstat "state"
text trkprom "prompt"
text trktool "tool"
text trkold "old"
text trknew "new"
text trmiss "missing"
text trrf "read_file"
text troc "omega_check"
text trcread "read"
text trcrepl "replace"
text trcchk "check"
text trloop "loop"
text tradd "add"
text trmul "mul"
text trdone "\nDone."
text trwork ".work"
text trcap ".tool-replay.out"
text trsel "/final-selected.json"
text trnull "/dev/null"
text trmagic "OMNT1"
text trtask "Task: "
text trfile "\nFile: "
text trgoal "\nGoal: "
text trstate "\nState: "
text trg1 "calc starts with x and adds "
text trg2 " exactly "
text trg3 " times in a for loop. main calls calc with "
text trg4 "calc returns x "
text trplus "plus "
text trtimes "times "
text trg5 ". main calls calc with "
text trdot "."
text trsrc "Source:\n"
text trres "Tool result: "
text trans "Answer:\n"
text trmis "MISMATCH "
text trstw " status "
text trnone "None"
text trwant "  want "
text trsum1 "TOOL-REPLAY runs="
text trsum2 " pass="
text trsum3 " fail="
text trsum4 " actions="
text trexit "exit "
text trtmo "timeout"
text trbadr "malformed record"
text trspawn "spawn error"
text trerr "ERROR "
text trejob "job fields"
text trepath "paths"
text tretree "tree setup"
text treturn "turns"
text treraw "raw"
text trejson "raw json"
text tretool "tool"
text treargv "arguments"
text trewant "next prompt"
text treload "tool-replay: cannot load ROUND40/final-selected.json\n"
text trusage "usage: tool-replay TOOL OMC ROUND40 OUTDIR\n"
note trsty1, trsty2: repair.py STYLES 0..25 and 26..50, one per line.
text trsty1 "Repair this Omega file and verify it.\nUse tools to fix this Omega program, then test it.\nCheck this Omega file, correct any fault and confirm the result.\nPlease get this Omega file working according to its goal and check your work.\nInvestigate this Omega file and make its behavior match the goal.\nDiagnose this Omega file, repair it as needed, and verify the result.\nRepair the calculation in this Omega file and verify the result.\nFind and repair the mistake in this Omega file, then confirm its behavior.\nMake this Omega file satisfy its stated goal and verify the repaired result.\nFix this Omega file.\nCheck and repair the Omega program.\nMake the program match its goal and test it.\nUse tools to repair the file and check it.\nFind the wrong calculation, fix it, and test it.\nInspect this program and fix the error.\nRead the file, check it, repair it, and test again.\nPlease correct the Omega calculation and verify it.\nRepair this file to meet the stated goal.\nWork through this Omega repair and check the result.\nCheck this Omega file, find the error, repair it and verify the result.\nPlease inspect this Omega program to repair the calculation and verify the result.\nUse the goal to fix this Omega file and verify the changes.\nPlease repair this Omega program to do what the goal asks.\nGet this Omega file to match the goal, then check the result.\nPlease carefully repair the calculation using tools and confirm that the tests pass.\nPlease carefully examine this Omega file and repair any calculation that does not match its goal.\n"
text trsty2 "Find the incorrect behavior in this Omega file, fix it, and test the result.\nInspect and repair this Omega file, then verify it.\nCorrect this Omega program according to its goal.\nFix the error in this Omega program and check the result.\nCheck this file and repair it to meet its goal.\nPlease fix this program to match its goal.\nCorrect the calculation in this Omega file.\nRead this program and repair its calculation.\nPlease check the code and fix the mistake.\nRepair the program according to the stated goal.\nUse the goal to correct this Omega calculation.\nFix the calculation and test the corrected program.\nPlease inspect the file and correct the error.\nCheck the calculation, make the repair, and verify it.\nMake this file behave as the goal describes.\nPlease correct this program and check your work.\nRepair this calculation, then confirm the result.\nRepair this file and confirm it meets the goal.\nCheck the Omega program and correct its calculation.\nInspect this file, fix its calculation, and verify it.\nMake this Omega program meet the goal, then test it.\nRepair the file and verify its goal.\nCheck the code, repair its fault, and test it.\nFix the error in this file and confirm its goal.\nInspect the code and repair it to satisfy the goal.\n"

note ======== Python str.strip whitespace and repr

note tr_cpn c: the byte length of the UTF-8 sequence led by c (1 for ASCII or a stray byte).
fn tr_cpn c uchar to ulong
if lt c 192
ret 1
end
if lt c 224
ret 2
end
if lt c 240
ret 3
end
if lt c 248
ret 4
end
ret 1
end

note tr_cp b i k: the code point of the k-byte (2..4) UTF-8 sequence at b[i].
fn tr_cp b view uchar 8192 i ulong k ulong to ulong
c = and ulong get b i shr 127 k
j = ulong 1
while lt j k bound 4
d = and ulong get b add i j 63
c = or shl c 6 d
j = add j 1
end
ret c
end

note tr_uws cp: whether non-ASCII code point cp is Python whitespace (str.isspace).
fn tr_uws cp ulong to bool
if or eq cp 133 eq cp 160
ret true
end
if eq cp 5760
ret true
end
if and ge cp 8192 le cp 8202
ret true
end
if or eq cp 8232 eq cp 8233
ret true
end
if or eq cp 8239 eq cp 8287
ret true
end
ret eq cp 12288
end

note tr_aws c: whether byte c is ASCII Python whitespace (\t \n \v \f \r, 0x1c..0x1f, space).
fn tr_aws c uchar to bool
ret or and ge c 9 le c 13 or eq c 32 and ge c 28 le c 31
end

note tr_wsat b i e: the byte length of the whitespace code point at b[i] (ending by e), or 0.
fn tr_wsat b view uchar 8192 i ulong e ulong to ulong
c = get b i
if tr_aws c
ret 1
end
k = tr_cpn c
if eq k 1
ret 0
end
if gt add i k e
ret 0
end
if tr_uws tr_cp b i k
ret k
end
ret 0
end

note tr_wsend b s e: the byte length of the whitespace code point ending at b[e] (e > s), or 0.
fn tr_wsend b view uchar 8192 s ulong e ulong to ulong
c = get b sub e 1
if lt c 128
if tr_aws c
ret 1
end
ret 0
end
j = sub e 1
while gt j s bound 4
d = get b j
if or lt d 128 gt d 191
break
end
if ge sub e j 4
break
end
j = sub j 1
end
k = tr_cpn get b j
if eq k 1
ret 0
end
if ne add j k e
ret 0
end
if tr_uws tr_cp b j k
ret k
end
ret 0
end

note tr_text rb n ib: raw.split('\nDone.')[0].strip() of rb[0, n) copied to ib[0, ..); its length.
fn tr_text rb view uchar 8192 n ulong ib edit uchar 8192 to ulong
e = dv_find part rb 0 n trdone 0
if eq e dvnone
e = n
end
s = ulong 0
while lt s e bound 8193
k = tr_wsat rb s e
if eq k 0
break
end
s = add s k
end
while gt e s bound 8193
k = tr_wsend rb s e
if eq k 0
break
end
e = sub e k
end
q = dv_cat ib 0 part rb s sub e s
ret sub e s
end

note tr_quote b: the quote Python repr uses for b: '"' when b holds a ' and no ", else '.
fn tr_quote b view uchar * to uchar
s1 = false
d1 = false
for i ulong len b
c = get b i
if eq c 39
s1 = true
end
if eq c 34
d1 = true
end
end
if and s1 not d1
ret 34
end
ret 39
end

note tr_rlen b i: the input bytes one repr step consumes at b[i] (a whole UTF-8 sequence).
fn tr_rlen b view uchar * i ulong to ulong
c = get b i
if lt c 128
ret 1
end
k = tr_cpn c
if gt k sub len b i
ret 1
end
ret k
end

note tr_hex t w c: "\xNN" (lower-case hex of c) at t[w]; w + 4.
fn tr_hex t edit uchar 65600 w ulong c uchar to ulong
put t w 92
put t add w 1 120
h = shr c 4
l = and c 15
if lt h 10
put t add w 2 add h 48
else
put t add w 2 add h 87
end
if lt l 10
put t add w 3 add l 48
else
put t add w 3 add l 87
end
ret add w 4
end

note tr_esc t w c: a backslash and c at t[w]; w + 2.
fn tr_esc t edit uchar 65600 w ulong c uchar to ulong
put t w 92
put t add w 1 c
ret add w 2
end

note tr_r1 t w b i q: the repr of the code point at b[i] (quote q) written at t[w]; the new w.
fn tr_r1 t edit uchar 65600 w ulong b view uchar * i ulong q uchar to ulong
c = get b i
if or eq c 92 eq c q
ret tr_esc t w c
end
if eq c 9
ret tr_esc t w 116
end
if eq c 10
ret tr_esc t w 110
end
if eq c 13
ret tr_esc t w 114
end
if or lt c 32 eq c 127
ret tr_hex t w c
end
if lt c 128
put t w c
ret add w 1
end
k = tr_rlen b i
if eq k 2
if eq c 194
d = get b add i 1
if or le d 160 eq d 173
ret tr_hex t w d
end
end
end
for j ulong k
put t add w j get b add i j
end
ret add w k
end

note tr_rfull t b: Python repr of the string b (UTF-8) written to t[0, ..); its length.
fn tr_rfull t edit uchar 65600 b view uchar * to ulong
q = tr_quote b
put t 0 q
w = ulong 1
i = ulong 0
while lt i len b bound 16777217
w = tr_r1 t w b i q
i = add i tr_rlen b i
end
put t w q
ret add w 1
end

note tr_rcut t n lim: the byte length of the first lim code points of t[0, n).
fn tr_rcut t view uchar 65600 n ulong lim ulong to ulong
c = ulong 0
i = ulong 0
while lt i n bound 65601
d = get t i
if or lt d 128 gt d 191
if eq c lim
ret i
end
c = add c 1
end
i = add i 1
end
ret n
end

note tr_repr o p b lim: repr(b)[:lim] appended at o[p] (dv_cat rules); the new end or dvnone.
note b is at most 16384 bytes.
fn tr_repr o edit uchar * p ulong b view uchar * lim ulong to ulong
t = new uchar 65600 0
n = tr_rfull t b
m = tr_rcut t n lim
ret dv_cat o p view part t 0 m
end

note tr_back b n k: the start of the last k code points of b[0, n) (0 when fewer).
fn tr_back b view uchar 16384 n ulong k ulong to ulong
i = n
c = ulong 0
while gt i 0 bound 16385
i = sub i 1
d = get b i
if or lt d 128 gt d 191
c = add c 1
if eq c k
ret i
end
end
end
ret 0
end

note ======== the job and its prompt head

note tr_line o p t k: line k of the newline-terminated lines t appended at o[p]; the end or dvnone.
fn tr_line o edit uchar * p ulong t view uchar * k ulong to ulong
i = ulong 0
c = ulong 0
s = ulong 0
while lt i len t bound 4096
if eq get t i 10
if eq c k
ret dv_cat o p part t s sub i s
end
c = add c 1
s = add i 1
end
i = add i 1
end
ret dvnone
end

note tr_style o p: STYLES[job.style] appended at o[p]; dvnone for a style outside 0..50.
fn tr_style o edit uchar * p ulong to ulong
s = get trv 0
if or lt s 0 gt s 50
ret dvnone
end
if lt s 26
ret tr_line o p trsty1 ulong s
end
ret tr_line o p trsty2 sub ulong s 26
end

note tr_goal o p: repair.py goal(job) appended at o[p]; the end or dvnone.
fn tr_goal o edit uchar * p ulong to ulong
if eq get trv 1 3
if eq get trv 5 0
ret dvnone
end
q = dv_cat o p trg1
q = dv_fmtl o q get trv 2
q = dv_cat o q trg2
q = dv_fmtl o q get trv 3
q = dv_cat o q trg3
q = dv_fmtl o q get trv 4
ret dv_cat o q trdot
end
q = dv_cat o p trg4
if eq get trv 1 1
q = dv_cat o q trplus
else
q = dv_cat o q trtimes
end
q = dv_fmtl o q get trv 2
q = dv_cat o q trg5
q = dv_fmtl o q get trv 4
ret dv_cat o q trdot
end

note tr_jint src tape v i: whether token v is an integer; stores it in trv[i].
fn tr_jint src view uchar * tape view uint dvtcap v ulong i ulong to bool
if not dv_jisl src tape v
ret false
end
put trv i dv_jnum src tape v
ret true
end

note tr_jnums src tape j: job style, kind, k, a and n (default 0) into trv; 0 or -1.
fn tr_jnums src view uchar * tape view uint dvtcap j ulong to long
if not tr_jint src tape dv_jkey src tape j trkstyl 0
ret neg long 1
end
if not tr_jint src tape dv_jkey src tape j trkk 2
ret neg long 1
end
if not tr_jint src tape dv_jkey src tape j trka 4
ret neg long 1
end
put trv 3 0
put trv 5 0
nv = dv_jkey src tape j trkn
if ne nv jsnone
if not tr_jint src tape nv 3
ret neg long 1
end
put trv 5 1
end
v = dv_jkey src tape j trkkind
put trv 1 0
if dv_jsteq src tape v tradd
put trv 1 1
end
if dv_jsteq src tape v trmul
put trv 1 2
end
if dv_jsteq src tape v trloop
put trv 1 3
end
ret 0
end

note tr_idok b: 0 when job id b is a single non-empty path component other than "." and "..".
fn tr_idok b view uchar * to long
n = len b
if eq n 0
ret neg long 1
end
for i ulong n
if or eq get b i 47 eq get b i 0
ret neg long 1
end
end
if eq get b 0 46
if eq n 1
ret neg long 1
end
if eq n 2
if eq get b 1 46
ret neg long 1
end
end
end
ret 0
end

note tr_job src tape j bj: job j's id, path, fault, broken (unless fault is "missing") into bj and
note its numbers into trv; 0 or -1.
fn tr_job src view uchar * tape view uint dvtcap j ulong bj edit uchar 16384 to long
v = dv_jkey src tape j trkid
n = dv_jstr src tape v part bj 0 1024
if lt n 0
ret neg long 1
end
put trb 0 ulong n
v = dv_jkey src tape j trkpath
n = dv_jstr src tape v part bj 1024 3072
if lt n 0
ret neg long 1
end
put trb 1 ulong n
v = dv_jkey src tape j trkflt
n = dv_jstr src tape v part bj 4096 1024
if lt n 0
ret neg long 1
end
put trb 2 ulong n
if lt tr_jnums src tape j 0
ret neg long 1
end
if not dv_eq view part bj 4096 get trb 2 trmiss
v = dv_jkey src tape j trkbrok
n = dv_jstr src tape v part bj 6144 6144
if lt n 0
ret neg long 1
end
put trb 3 ulong n
put trb 5 1
end
ret tr_idok view part bj 0 get trb 0
end

note tr_head ba bj: "Task: STYLE\nFile: PATH\nGoal: GOAL\nState: " into ba[24576, ..); 0 or -1.
fn tr_head ba edit uchar 32768 bj view uchar 16384 to long
o = new uchar 4096 0
p = dv_cat o 0 trtask
p = tr_style o p
p = dv_cat o p trfile
p = dv_cat o p part bj 1024 get trb 1
p = dv_cat o p trgoal
p = tr_goal o p
p = dv_cat o p trstate
if eq p dvnone
ret neg long 1
end
q = dv_cat part ba 24576 4096 0 view part o 0 p
put tra 6 p
ret 0
end

note tr_paths ba bj: ROOT = OUTDIR/id and WORK = ROOT/.work into ba, then the head; 0 or -1.
fn tr_paths ba edit uchar 32768 bj view uchar 16384 to long
t = new uchar 4096 0
n = dv_cat t 0 view part ba 8192 get tra 2
ni = get trb 0
r = dv_join part ba 12288 4096 view part t 0 n part bj 0 ni
if eq r dvnone
ret neg long 1
end
put tra 3 r
n = dv_cat t 0 view part ba 12288 r
r = dv_join part ba 16384 4096 view part t 0 n trwork
if eq r dvnone
ret neg long 1
end
put tra 4 r
ret tr_head ba bj
end

note tr_tree ba bj: rmtree(ROOT) (errors ignored), makedirs ROOT/dirname(path) and WORK, and the
note broken source written to ROOT/path; 0 or a negative error.
fn tr_tree ba view uchar 32768 bj view uchar 16384 to long
t = new uchar 4096 0
r = dv_rmrf part ba 12288 get tra 3
dn = dv_dirn part bj 1024 get trb 1
n = dv_join t part ba 12288 get tra 3 part bj 1024 dn
if eq n dvnone
ret neg long 36
end
r = dv_mkdirp view part t 0 n
if lt r 0
ret r
end
r = dv_mkdirp part ba 16384 get tra 4
if lt r 0
ret r
end
if eq get trb 5 0
ret 0
end
n = dv_join t part ba 12288 get tra 3 part bj 1024 get trb 1
if eq n dvnone
ret neg long 36
end
ret dv_spit view part t 0 n part bj 6144 get trb 3
end

note ======== one tool action

note tr_tcode bj: the tool of the current action: 1 read_file, 2 omega_check, 3 anything else.
fn tr_tcode bj view uchar 16384 to ulong
if dv_eq part bj 5120 get trb 4 trrf
ret 1
end
if dv_eq part bj 5120 get trb 4 troc
ret 2
end
ret 3
end

note tr_argc ba bj p: the check arguments WORK OMC KIND K N A appended to the packed list in bj.
fn tr_argc ba view uchar 32768 bj edit uchar 16384 p ulong to ulong
nb = new uchar 32 0
if eq get trv 1 0
ret dvnone
end
q = dv_pkadd part bj 12288 4096 p part ba 16384 get tra 4
q = dv_pkadd part bj 12288 4096 q part ba 4096 get tra 1
for i ulong 4
m = dv_fmtl nb 0 get trv add i 1
q = dv_pkadd part bj 12288 4096 q view part nb 0 m
end
ret q
end

note tr_argr bj p ib it: the replace arguments OLD NEW (strings of the parsed answer) appended.
fn tr_argr bj edit uchar 16384 p ulong ib view uchar 8192 it view uint dvtcap to ulong
ov = new uchar 4096 0
v = dv_jkey ib it 0 trkold
n = dv_jstr ib it v ov
if lt n 0
ret dvnone
end
q = dv_pkadd part bj 12288 4096 p view part ov 0 ulong n
v = dv_jkey ib it 0 trknew
n = dv_jstr ib it v ov
if lt n 0
ret dvnone
end
ret dv_pkadd part bj 12288 4096 q view part ov 0 ulong n
end

note tr_pkpa bj p pa n: pa[0, n) appended to the packed list in bj[12288, ..); as dv_pkadd.
fn tr_pkpa bj edit uchar 16384 p ulong pa view uchar 4096 n ulong to ulong
ret dv_pkadd part bj 12288 4096 p part pa 0 n
end

note tr_argv ba bj ib it: the TOOL command line of the parsed answer packed into bj[12288, ..);
note its length or dvnone.
fn tr_argv ba view uchar 32768 bj edit uchar 16384 ib view uchar 8192 it view uint dvtcap to ulong
pa = new uchar 4096 0
c = tr_tcode bj
p = dv_pkinit part bj 12288 4096
p = dv_pkadd part bj 12288 4096 p part ba 0 get tra 0
if eq c 1
p = dv_pkadd part bj 12288 4096 p trcread
end
if eq c 2
p = dv_pkadd part bj 12288 4096 p trcchk
end
if eq c 3
p = dv_pkadd part bj 12288 4096 p trcrepl
end
p = dv_pkadd part bj 12288 4096 p part ba 12288 get tra 3
n = dv_jstr ib it dv_jkey ib it 0 trkpath pa
if lt n 0
ret dvnone
end
p = tr_pkpa bj p pa ulong n
if eq c 2
ret tr_argc ba bj p
end
if eq c 3
ret tr_argr bj p ib it
end
ret p
end

note tr_split ob e fs: the ASCII-whitespace-separated fields of ob[0, e): the first four as
note (start, length) pairs in fs; the field count.
fn tr_split ob view uchar 16384 e ulong fs edit ulong 8 to ulong
k = ulong 0
s = ulong 0
inw = false
i = ulong 0
while lt i e bound 16385
if tr_aws get ob i
if inw
if lt k 4
put fs mul k 2 s
put fs add mul k 2 1 sub i s
end
k = add k 1
inw = false
end
else
if not inw
s = i
inw = true
end
end
i = add i 1
end
if inw
if lt k 4
put fs mul k 2 s
put fs add mul k 2 1 sub e s
end
k = add k 1
end
ret k
end

note tr_parse ob n: whether ob[0, n) is "OMNT1 st ol cl\n" then ol + cl body bytes; sets trs.
fn tr_parse ob view uchar 16384 n ulong to bool
fs = new ulong 8 0
nl = dv_find part ob 0 n dvnl 0
if eq nl dvnone
ret false
end
if lt tr_split ob nl fs 4
ret false
end
if not dv_eq part ob get fs 0 get fs 1 trmagic
ret false
end
st = dv_atou part ob get fs 2 get fs 3
ol = dv_atou part ob get fs 4 get fs 5
cl = dv_atou part ob get fs 6 get fs 7
if or or eq st dvnone eq ol dvnone eq cl dvnone
ret false
end
bl = sub sub n nl 1
if gt ol bl
ret false
end
if ne cl sub bl ol
ret false
end
put trs 0 st
put trs 1 add nl 1
put trs 2 ol
put trs 3 add add nl 1 ol
put trs 4 cl
if eq st 1
put trs 4 0
end
ret true
end

note tr_none ob w: observation for an action without a record into ob and trs (status None):
note w 0..255 "exit w", 256 + s "exit -s", -110 "timeout", -1000 "malformed record", else
note "spawn error".
fn tr_none ob edit uchar 16384 w long to void
n = ulong 0
if ge w 0
n = dv_cat ob 0 trexit
if gt w 255
n = dv_byte ob n 45
n = dv_fmtl ob n sub w 256
else
n = dv_fmtl ob n w
end
else
if eq w -110
n = dv_cat ob 0 trtmo
else
if eq w -1000
n = dv_cat ob 0 trbadr
else
n = dv_cat ob 0 trspawn
end
end
end
put trs 0 dvnone
put trs 1 0
put trs 2 n
put trs 3 0
put trs 4 0
end

note tr_got gb ba src tape: the head and the next turn's state and a newline into gb; end or dvnone.
fn tr_got gb edit uchar 16384 ba view uchar 32768 src view uchar * tape view uint dvtcap to ulong
sv = dv_jkey src tape get trs 5 trkstat
p = dv_cat gb 0 part ba 24576 get tra 6
n = dv_jstr src tape sv part gb p sub 16384 p
if lt n 0
ret dvnone
end
ret dv_byte gb add p ulong n 10
end

note tr_tail gb p ob: [Source:\n CONTENT][Tool result: OBS\n]Answer:\n appended at gb[p].
fn tr_tail gb edit uchar 16384 p ulong ob view uchar 16384 to ulong
q = p
if gt get trs 4 0
q = dv_cat gb q trsrc
q = dv_cat gb q part ob get trs 3 get trs 4
end
if gt get trs 2 0
q = dv_cat gb q trres
q = dv_cat gb q part ob get trs 1 get trs 2
q = dv_byte gb q 10
end
ret dv_cat gb q trans
end

note tr_miss bj ob: print "MISMATCH id fault tool status ST REPR" (REPR: repr(obs)[:200]).
fn tr_miss bj view uchar 16384 ob view uchar 16384 to void
o = new uchar 8192 0
p = dv_cat o 0 trmis
p = dv_cat o p part bj 0 get trb 0
p = dv_byte o p 32
p = dv_cat o p part bj 4096 get trb 2
p = dv_byte o p 32
p = dv_cat o p part bj 5120 get trb 4
p = dv_cat o p trstw
if eq get trs 0 dvnone
p = dv_cat o p trnone
else
p = dv_fmtu o p get trs 0
end
p = dv_byte o p 32
p = tr_repr o p part ob get trs 1 get trs 2 200
p = dv_byte o p 10
if ne p dvnone
x = dv_out view part o 0 p
end
end

note tr_wline wb wn: print "  want REPR" (REPR: repr of the last 200 code points of wb[0, wn)).
fn tr_wline wb view uchar 16384 wn ulong to void
o = new uchar 2048 0
s = tr_back wb wn 200
p = dv_cat o 0 trwant
p = tr_repr o p part wb s sub wn s 1000
p = dv_byte o p 10
if ne p dvnone
x = dv_out view part o 0 p
end
end

note tr_bad bj m: print "ERROR id m"; 1 (a failed run).
fn tr_bad bj view uchar 16384 m view uchar * to long
o = new uchar 4096 0
p = dv_cat o 0 trerr
p = dv_cat o p part bj 0 get trb 0
p = dv_byte o p 32
p = dv_cat o p m
p = dv_byte o p 10
if ne p dvnone
x = dv_out view part o 0 p
end
ret 1
end

note tr_same gb p wb wn: whether gb[0, p) (p not dvnone) equals wb[0, wn).
fn tr_same gb view uchar 16384 p ulong wb view uchar 16384 wn ulong to bool
if eq p dvnone
ret false
end
ret dv_eq part gb 0 p part wb 0 wn
end

note tr_judge ob src tape ba bj: rebuild the prompt from the observation in ob and trs and compare
note it with the next turn's prompt; 0 equal, 1 different (MISMATCH printed) or a fixture error.
fn tr_judge ob view uchar 16384 src view uchar * tape view uint dvtcap ba view uchar 32768 bj view uchar 16384 to long
gb = new uchar 16384 0
wb = new uchar 16384 0
p = tr_got gb ba src tape
p = tr_tail gb p ob
wn = dv_jstr src tape dv_jkey src tape get trs 5 trkprom wb
if lt wn 0
ret tr_bad bj trewant
end
if tr_same gb p wb ulong wn
ret 0
end
tr_miss bj ob
tr_wline wb ulong wn
ret 1
end

note tr_act ba bj ob: run the packed TOOL command (stdout to the capture file, stderr to /dev/null,
note 120 s deadline) and leave its observation in ob and trs.
fn tr_act ba view uchar 32768 bj view uchar 16384 ob edit uchar 16384 to void
pl = get trs 6
cl = get tra 5
pid = dv_spawn part bj 12288 pl part ba 20480 cl trnull
w = neg long 1
if ge pid 0
w = dv_wait pid 120000000000
end
if ne w 0
tr_none ob w
ret
end
n = dv_slurp part ba 20480 cl ob
if lt n 0
tr_none ob -1000
ret
end
if not tr_parse ob ulong n
tr_none ob -1000
end
end

note tr_exec src tape ba bj: run the packed TOOL command, read its record, judge; as tr_judge.
fn tr_exec src view uchar * tape view uint dvtcap ba view uchar 32768 bj view uchar 16384 to long
ob = new uchar 16384 0
tr_act ba bj ob
put trn 3 add get trn 3 1
ret tr_judge ob src tape ba bj
end

note tr_raw src tape t ib: turn t's raw answer cut and stripped into ib; its length, or -1.
fn tr_raw src view uchar * tape view uint dvtcap t ulong ib edit uchar 8192 to long
rb = new uchar 8192 0
n = dv_jstr src tape dv_jkey src tape t trkraw rb
if lt n 0
ret n
end
ret long tr_text rb ulong n ib
end

note tr_ans ib it m ba bj: parse the answer ib[0, m), store its tool name and pack its TOOL
note command line into bj; 0, or 1 after an ERROR line.
fn tr_ans ib view uchar 8192 it edit uint dvtcap m ulong ba view uchar 32768 bj edit uchar 16384 to long
r = js_init it jsmaxn 64
if lt r 0
ret tr_bad bj trejson
end
r = js_parse ib it m
if lt r 0
ret tr_bad bj trejson
end
k = dv_jstr ib it dv_jkey ib it 0 trktool part bj 5120 1024
if lt k 0
ret tr_bad bj tretool
end
put trb 4 ulong k
p = tr_argv ba bj ib it
if eq p dvnone
ret tr_bad bj treargv
end
put trs 6 p
ret 0
end

note tr_turn src tape t ba bj: the action of turn t judged against the following turn; as tr_judge.
fn tr_turn src view uchar * tape view uint dvtcap t ulong ba view uchar 32768 bj edit uchar 16384 to long
ib = new uchar 8192 0
it = new uint dvtcap 0
put trs 5 js_enext tape t
m = tr_raw src tape t ib
if lt m 0
ret tr_bad bj treraw
end
if ne tr_ans ib it ulong m ba bj 0
ret 1
end
ret tr_exec src tape ba bj
end

note tr_run src tape r ba bj: replay run r; 0 passed, 1 failed.
fn tr_run src view uchar * tape view uint dvtcap r ulong ba edit uchar 32768 bj edit uchar 16384 to long
for i ulong 8
put trb i 0
end
j = dv_jkey src tape r trkjob
if lt tr_job src tape j bj 0
ret tr_bad bj trejob
end
if lt tr_paths ba bj 0
ret tr_bad bj trepath
end
if lt tr_tree ba bj 0
ret tr_bad bj tretree
end
tv = dv_jkey src tape r trkturn
if ne js_type tape tv jsarr
ret tr_bad bj treturn
end
t = js_first tape tv
while ne t jsnone bound 16777216
nx = js_enext tape t
if eq nx jsnone
ret 0
end
if ne tr_turn src tape t ba bj 0
ret 1
end
t = nx
end
ret 0
end

note tr_args ba: TOOL, OMC, OUTDIR, ROUND40/final-selected.json and OUTDIR/.tool-replay.out into ba.
fn tr_args ba edit uchar 32768 to long
t = new uchar 4096 0
n = dv_arg 1 part ba 0 4095
if lt n 0
ret n
end
put tra 0 ulong n
n = dv_arg 2 part ba 4096 4095
if lt n 0
ret n
end
put tra 1 ulong n
n = dv_arg 4 part ba 8192 4095
if lt n 0
ret n
end
put tra 2 ulong n
n = dv_arg 3 part ba 28672 4095
if lt n 0
ret n
end
q = dv_cat part ba 28672 4095 ulong n trsel
if eq q dvnone
ret neg long 36
end
put tra 7 q
q = dv_cat t 0 view part ba 8192 get tra 2
q = dv_join part ba 20480 4095 view part t 0 q trcap
if eq q dvnone
ret neg long 36
end
put tra 5 q
ret 0
end

note tr_sum: print "TOOL-REPLAY runs=N pass=P fail=F actions=A".
fn tr_sum to void
o = new uchar 256 0
p = dv_cat o 0 trsum1
p = dv_fmtu o p get trn 0
p = dv_cat o p trsum2
p = dv_fmtu o p get trn 1
p = dv_cat o p trsum3
p = dv_fmtu o p get trn 2
p = dv_cat o p trsum4
p = dv_fmtu o p get trn 3
p = dv_byte o p 10
x = dv_out view part o 0 p
end

fn main to int
src = new uchar 983040 0
tape = new uint dvtcap 0
ba = new uchar 32768 0
bj = new uchar 16384 0
if lt dv_argc 5
x = dv_err trusage
ret 2
end
if lt tr_args ba 0
x = dv_err trusage
ret 2
end
n = dv_jload view part ba 28672 get tra 7 src tape
if lt n 0
x = dv_err treload
ret 2
end
if ne js_type tape 0 jsarr
x = dv_err treload
ret 2
end
r = js_first tape 0
while ne r jsnone bound 16777216
f = tr_run src tape r ba bj
put trn 0 add get trn 0 1
if eq f 0
put trn 1 add get trn 1 1
else
put trn 2 add get trn 2 1
end
r = js_enext tape r
end
u = unlink ba 20480 get tra 5
tr_sum
if eq get trn 2 0
ret 0
end
ret 1
end
